---

<BaseLayout centered title="about">
  <div class="home about-page">
    <div class="about-intro">
      <img
        class="about-portrait"
        src="/headshots/studio-projection-small.webp"
        alt="Spencer standing in a studio, lit by colorful projected lines"
        width="1500"
        height="1125"
      />
      <div class="about-statement">
        <p class="about-lede">
          Spencer Chang makes <a
            href="https://news.spencer.place/p/software-you-can-touch"
            >software we can touch</a
          >, like <a
            href="https://www.are.na/spencer-chang/communal-computing-infrastructure"
            >communal computers</a
          >, <a href="https://internetsculptures.com">internet objects</a>, and <a
            href="/creation/playhtml">online spaces</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>These include:</p>
        <ol class="about-kinds">
          <!-- TODO: add floating image hover preview for each of these, support for hosted creations to show their preview -->
          <li>
            <span class="about-kind">infrastructure</span>
            <span>
              <a href="/creation/playhtml">creative tools</a>,
              <a href="/creation/touching-computers-creating-data-talismans"
                >experimental interfaces</a
              >,
              <a href="/creation/gather">local-first apps</a>,
              <a href="/creation/verses-verses">text playgrounds</a>,
              <a href="/creation/i-love-living">archival automations</a>,
              <a href="/creation/syllabus-taking-an-internet-walk"
                >instruction manuals</a
              >
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="about-kind">environments</span>
            <span>
              <a href="/creation/html-garden">living ecosystems</a>,
              <a href="/creation/poems-we-found-with-the-internet"
                >playful spaces</a
              >,
              <a href="/creation/everyday">phone interventions</a>,
              <a href="/creation/cursor-watching">live windows</a>,
              <a href="/creation/neighborhood-internets-workshop"
                >creating neighborhood internets</a
              >,
              <a href="/creation/(we)bsite">collections of dreams</a>,
              <a href="/creation/8-bite">games</a>
            </span>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p id="expandingWork"></p>
    <script define:vars={{ workDescription }}>
      let node = createTelescopicTextFromBulletedList(workDescription, {
        textMode: TextMode.Html,
      });
      const container = document.getElementById("expandingWork");
      container.appendChild(node);
    </script>

    <p>
      They are open to collaborations <span class="aside"
        >(with people or brands)</span
      >, invitations <span class="aside">(to teach or speak)</span>, and
      commissions <span class="aside"
        >(of objects or digital experiences)</span
      >. Say hi to them <a href="mailto:spencer@spencer.place?subject=collab%20pls"
        >over email</a
      > or <a href="/collab">learn more</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      For a professional statement, bio, and full work information, see the <a
        href="/cv">CV</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2 class="about-heading">some questions &amp; ever-evolving answers</h2>
    <div class="about-questions">
      <details>
        <summary> 1. why the internet? </summary>
        <p>
          Growing up, I never felt like I fit in at school or local communities.
          Instead, I grew up on the internet. The internet was where I found my
          community, learned what it meant to have a passion, and discovered the
          range of humanity—how tender and how heartless people could be.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because of this, I am driven to understand and create spaces that
          allow for people to be seen: their lives, sorrows, and dreams. The
          internet is increasingly the medium for this, from our constant
          encounters with the supercomputers in our pockets to the pleas to be
          seen in every comment and corner of the web. Grappling directly with
          the tension between the oppressive bases of technology and its role as
          a global source for connection, meaning, and agency, my work
          speculates what the internet might look like if these were in harmony
          by offering living systems that do so. Varying between spaces that
          invite new ways for seeing each other digitally, tools for creating
          new methods of connection, and objects that inspire whimsical intimacy
          with our devices, I am always in search of a form of technology that
          lives as we do.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary> 2. what is your goal? </summary>
        <p>
          That we live in a world where the technology we make and advance feels
          as fundamentally human as humanities or cultural work. That we live in
          a world where we aren't trying to get away from our phones and remove
          technology, where our idea of technology is not so dominated by
          capitalism and surveillance, where it can be used for fun things,
          poetic things, things that have no reason for existing other than the
          fact that someone wanted them to. A world where technology is as
          natural a medium for bringing us closer together as public space is.
        </p>
        <p>
          In practical terms, I'm still not really sure what the end steady
          state of this work looks like, but I have inspirations: Noguchi,
          Fluxus, MSCHF, Bluesky. A full-time artist <Footnote
            client:only="react"
            url="https://americanartist.us/">*</Footnote
          >? An indie game/product studio<Footnote
            client:only="react"
            url="https://panic.com/">*</Footnote
          >? An experimental research group<Footnote
            client:only="react"
            url="http://inkandswitch.com">*1</Footnote
          ><Footnote client:only="react" url="https://modemworks.com/"
            >*2</Footnote
          >? An independent software creative<Footnote
            client:only="react"
            url="https://tarng.com/">*</Footnote
          >? If you have ideas or thoughts or if you're going through a similar
          journey, I'd love <a
            href="mailto:spencer@spencer.place?subject=MAKING A LIVING DOING WHAT YOU LOVE IS HARD!!!"
            >to chat</a
          >.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary> 3. what do you enjoy?</summary>
        <p id="expandingLikes"></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary> 4. why orange?</summary>
        <p>
          I like how radiant it is, how it is equally found in nature (sunsets,
          poppies, delicious fruit) and in our built environment (contemporary
          objects, industry, and warm lighting). It can be striking yet still
          welcoming, signal play while being couragerous and poised. I've always
          loved it, but I hid it as a child because I didn't want to stand out.
          Now, I like how different it is. Someone told me that orange is one
          the of the least favorite colors, so it's also nice to bond with
          others who love it.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <p class="descriptionText">
      p.s. like these highlighted paragraphs that expand when you touch them?
      they're made with the <a href="/creation/verses-verses"
        >open-source library</a
      > jacky and I made.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Guestbook client:only="react" />
  <br />


  <style is:global>
    /* Page-scoped, following the proposed site design system
       : Vulf Sans for body, Cooper only for the one display
       statement, 1.25 type scale. Values are literal because Tailwind (loaded
       on this page) already defines --text-*, --font-* and --radius-* vars. */
    /* Not using .headerContainer: it @extends .serif, which forces Cooper
       onto every paragraph. .home sets 18px, hence the doubled class. */
    .home.about-page {
      font-family: "Vulf Sans", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 3em 0 24px;
    }

    .about-page p {
      margin: 12px 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 500px) {
      .about-page {
        margin-top: 0.5em;
      }
    }

    .about-page .about-intro {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(200px, 300px) 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
      align-items: start;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .about-page .about-portrait {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      max-height: 45vh;
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: 50% 35%;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .about-page .about-lede {
      font-family: "Cooper", serif;
      font-size: 1.5625rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .about-page .about-kinds {
      list-style: decimal;
      padding-left: 1.25em;
      margin: 12px 0;
    }

    .about-page .about-kinds li + li {
      margin-top: 0.5em;
    }

    .about-page .about-kind {
      font-weight: 500;
    }

    .about-page .about-kind::after {
      content: ":";
    }

    .about-page .aside {
      font-style: italic;
    }

    /* Project names inside the expanding text keep their colors but use the
       page's typeface instead of one-off fonts. */
    .about-page #expandingWork #coda,
    .about-page #expandingWork #verses {
      font-family: inherit;
      font-size: inherit;
      font-style: normal;
    }

    .about-page .about-heading {
      font-family: "Vulf Sans", sans-serif;
      font-size: 1.5625rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin: 2em 0 0.75em;
    }

    .about-page .about-questions {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .about-page .about-questions summary {
      cursor: pointer;
      font-size: inherit;
    }

    .about-page .descriptionText {
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      color: #6b665c;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .about-page .about-intro {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 1.25rem;
      }

      .about-page .about-portrait {
        aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Likes logic -->
  <script define:vars={{ likesData: likes, enjoyPrompt }}>
    // TODO: can you add hover tooltips with images and previews?
    // TODO: support descriptors for each in the list, and have a way to "ellipsis" to add a new of the top level one
    // 'in my room', 'snuggled in quiet corners', 'in public parks'
    // randomize likes
    let likes = likesData;
    likes = likes.sort(() => Math.random() - 0.5);
    likes.splice(12, 0, [enjoyPrompt]);
    let likeExpandedIdx = 0;

    function createLikeNode(like) {
      const likeNode = document.createElement("span");
      likeNode.classList.add("likeItem");
      likeNode.innerHTML = `${like}`;
      if (likeExpandedIdx < likes.length - 1) {
        likeNode.innerHTML += ", ";
      }
      if (likeExpandedIdx === likes.length - 2) {
        likeNode.innerHTML += "and ";
      }
      return likeNode;
    }
    const likesNode = document.createElement("div");
    likesNode.id = "telescope";
    likesNode.style.display = "inline";
    const onMoreNode = document.createElement("div");
    onMoreNode.style = "display: inline-block;";
    onMoreNode.setAttribute("role", "button");
    onMoreNode.setAttribute("tabindex", "0");
    onMoreNode.setAttribute(
      "title",
      "click me to see more! try tabbing to me and using enter or space to go even faster!",
    );
    onMoreNode.innerHTML = "and...";
    onMoreNode.addEventListener("click", onClickMore);
    onMoreNode.addEventListener("keydown", onKeyDown);
    const likesContainer = document.getElementById("expandingLikes");
    likesContainer.appendChild(likesNode);
    likesNode.appendChild(
      document.createTextNode("A non-exhaustive list of the things I enjoy:"),
    );
    likesNode.appendChild(document.createElement("br"));
    likesNode.appendChild(onMoreNode);
    onMoreNode.classList.add("details");
    onMoreNode.classList.add("close");

    function onKeyDown(e) {
      if (event.key === "Enter" || event.key === " ") {
        onClickMore();
        e.preventDefault();
      }
    }

    function onClickMore() {
      const likeNode = createLikeNode(likes[likeExpandedIdx]);
      likesNode.insertBefore(likeNode, onMoreNode);
      likeExpandedIdx++;
      if (likeExpandedIdx === likes.length) {
        onMoreNode.remove();
        return;
      }
    }
    // start with 3 open
    onClickMore();
    onClickMore();
    onClickMore();
    onClickMore();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
